messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIt\'s impossible for the Lakers to make it to the finals. If the Lakers reach the finals, then the sun will come out from the west.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is most similar to the above argument?\n# Options:\nA) It\'s not cold today. if it\'s cold, why is the lake frozen?\nB) Language cannot create wealth. if language can create wealth, then the boastful person is the richest in the world.\nC) Plants are soft and fragile when they grow and become dry and haggard when they die. so strong things belong to the kind of death, weak things belong to the kind of growth.\nD) There is no pie in the sky. if you don\'t believe this, you will be deceived sooner or later.\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given context and question step by step.\n\n1. **Context Analysis:**\n   - The context states: "It\'s impossible for the Lakers to make it to the finals."\n   - It also states: "If the Lakers reach the finals, then the sun will come out from the west."\n\n2. **Identifying the Logical Structure:**\n   - The context presents a conditional statement: "If the Lakers reach the finals, then the sun will come out from the west."\n   - The impossibility of the Lakers reaching the finals is used to infer that the second part of the conditional statement (the sun coming out from the west) cannot be true.\n\n3. **Question Analysis:**\n   - The question asks us to find an option that is most similar to the given argument.\n   - We need to identify an option where the first part of a conditional statement is impossible, leading to the conclusion that the second part of the conditional statement cannot be true.\n\n4. **Option Analysis:**\n   - **Option A:** "It\'s not cold today. if it\'s cold, why is the lake frozen?"\n     - This option does not present a conditional statement. It is a question about the lake being frozen when it should not be.\n   - **Option B:** "Language cannot create wealth. if language can create wealth, then the boastful person is the richest in the world."\n     - This option presents a conditional statement: "If language can create wealth, then the boastful person is the richest in the world."\n     - The impossibility of language creating wealth leads to the conclusion that the boastful person cannot be the richest in the world.\n   - **Option C:** "Plants are soft and fragile when they grow and become dry and haggard when they die. so strong things belong to the kind of death, weak things belong to the kind of growth."\n     - This option does not present a conditional statement. It is a general statement about plant growth and death.\n   - **Option D:** "There is no pie in the sky. if you don\'t believe this, you will be deceived sooner or later."\n     - This option does not present a conditional statement. It is a statement about belief and deception.\n\n5. **Conclusion:**\n   - Option B is the most similar to the given argument because it presents a conditional statement where the first part (language cannot create wealth) is impossible, leading to the conclusion that the second part (the boastful person is the richest in the world) cannot be true.\nThe correct option is:']
