messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA committee works for two years and is composed of 4 members each year, 2 of which are from the following 4 judges: F, G, H and I, and the other 2 members are from the following 3 scientists: V, Y and Z. Each year, the committee is chaired by one member. A member who chairs the first year must retire from the committee during the second year. The person who chairs the second year must be a member of the committee during the first year. The committee members must meet the following conditions: G and V cannot be members of the committee in the same year. H and Y cannot be members of this committee in the same year. Each year, only one of I and V is a member of this committee.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if H is the chairman in the first year, which of the followings can be the chairman in the second year?\n# Options:\nA) F\nB) G\nC) Y\nD) I\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the given information and constraints step by step:\n\n1. **Committee Composition:**\n   - 4 members each year: 2 judges (F, G, H, I) and 2 scientists (V, Y, Z).\n   - 2 judges and 2 scientists each year.\n   - Each year, the committee is chaired by one member.\n\n2. **Chairman Conditions:**\n   - A member who chairs the first year must retire from the committee during the second year.\n   - The person who chairs the second year must be a member of the committee during the first year.\n   - G and V cannot be members of the committee in the same year.\n   - H and Y cannot be members of the committee in the same year.\n   - Each year, only one of I and V is a member of the committee.\n\n3. **Given Information:**\n   - H is the chairman in the first year.\n   - H and Y cannot be members of the committee in the same year.\n   - G and V cannot be members of the committee in the same year.\n   - Only one of I and V is a member of the committee each year.\n\n4. **First Year:**\n   - H is the chairman.\n   - H and Y cannot be in the same year, so Y cannot be a member.\n   - G and V cannot be in the same year, so if G is a member, V cannot be a member.\n   - Only one of I and V is a member, so if I is a member, V cannot be a member, and vice versa.\n\n5. **Second Year:**\n   - The second year's chairman must be a member of the committee in the first year.\n   - H is the chairman in the first year, so the second year's chairman must be one of the members of the first year's committee (F, G, I, or V).\n\n6. **Analyzing the Options:**\n   - **Option A: F**\n     - F can be a member of the first year's committee if G is not a member (since G and V cannot be in the same year).\n     - F can be a member of the second year's committee if G is not a member.\n     - This is possible.\n   \n   - **Option B: G**\n     - G cannot be a member of the first year's committee because H and Y cannot be in the same year.\n     - G cannot be a member of the second year's committee because G and V cannot be in the same year.\n     - This is not possible.\n   \n   - **Option C: Y**\n     - Y cannot be a member of the first year's committee.\n     - Y cannot be a member of the second year's committee because H and Y cannot be in the same year.\n     - This is not possible.\n   \n   - **Option D: I**\n     - I can be a member of the first year's committee if V is not a member (since only one of I and V is a member each year).\n     - I can be a member of the second year's committee if V is not a member.\n     - This is possible.\nThe correct option is:"]
