messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe mobile phone usage of the administrative department of a company is as follows: 1. Xiao Wang dialed the phone of everyone in the administrative department; 2. Xiao Li once called Xiao Zhao, but Xiao Zhao never called anyone else; 3. People who have never answered calls from others in the administration department have never called others.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings can be infered:\n# Options:\nA) Xiao zhao never answered a phone call from xiao li\nB) Xiao li once answered a phone call from xiao wang\nC) Someone in the administration department once called xiao wang\nD) Xiao wang answered the phone from everyone in the administration department\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the given information and analyze each statement step by step:\n\n1. **Xiao Wang dialed the phone of everyone in the administrative department.**\n   - This means Xiao Wang made calls to all members of the administrative department.\n\n2. **Xiao Li once called Xiao Zhao, but Xiao Zhao never called anyone else.**\n   - Xiao Li made a call to Xiao Zhao.\n   - Xiao Zhao did not make any calls to anyone else in the administrative department.\n\n3. **People who have never answered calls from others in the administration department have never called others.**\n   - This implies that if someone has never received a call from another person, they have not made any calls to others.\n\nNow, let's evaluate each option based on the given information:\n\n**Option A: Xiao Zhao never answered a phone call from Xiao Li**\n- We know Xiao Li called Xiao Zhao, but we do not have information about whether Xiao Zhao answered the call or not. Therefore, we cannot infer this statement.\n\n**Option B: Xiao Li once answered a phone call from Xiao Wang**\n- Xiao Li called Xiao Zhao, but there is no information about Xiao Li answering a call from Xiao Wang. Therefore, we cannot infer this statement.\n\n**Option C: Someone in the administration department once called Xiao Wang**\n- Xiao Wang dialed the phone of everyone in the administrative department, which means Xiao Wang made calls to all members. Therefore, someone in the administration department (Xiao Wang himself) did call Xiao Wang. This statement can be inferred.\n\n**Option D: Xiao Wang answered the phone from everyone in the administration department**\n- Xiao Wang dialed the phone of everyone in the administrative department, but we do not have information about whether Xiao Wang answered each call. Therefore, we cannot infer this statement.\nThe correct option is:"]
