messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nSome students attending a small university with a well-known choir live off campus. From the fact that all music majors are members of the choir, a professor in the music department concluded that none of the students who live off campus is a music major.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, the professor\'s conclusion is properly drawn if which one of the following is assumed?\n# Options:\nA) None of the students who live off campus is a member of the choir.\nB) All students who are members of the choir are music majors.\nC) Some of the students who do not live off campus are not music majors.\nD) All students who live on campus are music majors.\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given context and the professor\'s conclusion step by step.\n\n1. **Context Analysis:**\n   - Some students attending a small university with a well-known choir live off campus.\n   - All music majors are members of the choir.\n\n2. **Professor\'s Conclusion:**\n   - The professor concluded that none of the students who live off campus is a music major.\n\n3. **Logical Reasoning:**\n   - We need to determine if the professor\'s conclusion logically follows from the given information.\n   - The professor\'s conclusion is: "None of the students who live off campus is a music major."\n   - To verify this, we need to check if the given information supports this conclusion.\n\n4. **Assumptions:**\n   - We need to identify any assumptions that must be true for the professor\'s conclusion to be valid.\n   - Let\'s examine each option to see if it is necessary for the conclusion to hold.\n\n5. **Option Analysis:**\n   - **Option A: None of the students who live off campus is a member of the choir.**\n     - This option is not necessary. The professor\'s conclusion does not depend on whether students who live off campus are members of the choir or not. It only depends on whether they are music majors.\n   - **Option B: All students who are members of the choir are music majors.**\n     - This option is not necessary. The professor\'s conclusion does not require that all choir members are music majors. It only needs to be true that all music majors are choir members.\n   - **Option C: Some of the students who do not live off campus are not music majors.**\n     - This option is not necessary. The professor\'s conclusion does not depend on the status of students who live on campus. It only concerns students who live off campus.\n   - **Option D: All students who live on campus are music majors.**\n     - This option is necessary. If all students who live on campus are music majors, then none of the students who live off campus can be music majors, as the professor\'s conclusion states.\n\n6. **Conclusion:**\n   - The professor\'s conclusion that "none of the students who live off campus is a music major" is properly drawn if the assumption that "all students who live on campus are music majors" is true.\nThe correct option is:']
