messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe amount of time it takes for most of a worker\'s occupational knowledge and skills to become obsolete has been declining because of the introduction of advanced manufacturing technology (AMT). Given the rate at which AMT is currently being introduced in manufacturing, the average worker\'s old skills become obsolete and new skills are required within as little as five years.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following plans, if feasible, would allow a company to prepare most effectively for the rapid obsolescence of skills described above?\n# Options:\nA) The company will ensure that it can offer its employees any training necessary for meeting their job requirements.\nB) The company will develop a program to offer selected employees the opportunity to receive training six years after they were originally hired.\nC) The company will increase its investment in amt every year for a period of at least five years.\nD) The company will periodically survey its employees to determine how the introduction of amt has affected them.\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step:\n\n1. **Context Analysis**:\n   - The context states that the amount of time it takes for a worker\'s occupational knowledge and skills to become obsolete is decreasing due to the introduction of advanced manufacturing technology (AMT).\n   - It specifically mentions that new skills are required within as little as five years for most workers.\n\n2. **Question Analysis**:\n   - The question asks for a plan that would allow a company to prepare most effectively for the rapid obsolescence of skills described above.\n\n3. **Option Analysis**:\n   - **Option A**: "The company will ensure that it can offer its employees any training necessary for meeting their job requirements."\n     - This option aligns well with the context. Since skills become obsolete quickly, the company needs to be able to provide ongoing training to keep employees\' skills up-to-date.\n   - **Option B**: "The company will develop a program to offer selected employees the opportunity to receive training six years after they were originally hired."\n     - This option is not ideal because it suggests training will be offered six years after the original hiring date, which is more than the five years mentioned in the context. This would not effectively prepare employees for the rapid obsolescence of skills.\n   - **Option C**: "The company will increase its investment in AMT every year for a period of at least five years."\n     - While increasing investment in AMT is important, it does not directly address the need for training to keep skills current. The context emphasizes the need for training to adapt to the rapid obsolescence of skills.\n   - **Option D**: "The company will periodically survey its employees to determine how the introduction of AMT has affected them."\n     - This option is about monitoring the impact of AMT on employees but does not directly address the need for training to keep skills current. It is more about understanding the situation rather than preparing for it.\nThe correct option is:']
