messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe prehistoric fish Tiktaalik is the earliest known animal with fingers. Since variations were so great among prehistoric fish species, Tiktaalik would not have stood out as unusual at the time. However, Tiktaalik\' s fingers were an important development in animal evolution because it is likely that Tiktaalik is an ancestor to the many land animals with fingers.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, the statements above, if true, most strongly support which one of the following?\n# Options:\nA) Tiktaalik is not the ancestor of any currently surviving fish species.\nB) Tiktaalik\'s fingers were its only feature to play a significant role in the development of modern land animals.\nC) The evolutionary significance of tiktaalik could not be determined just through comparison to fish species of its time.\nD) No fish without fingers would ever be able to move on land.\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and analyze each option step by step:\n\n1. **Context Analysis**:\n   - Tiktaalik is the earliest known animal with fingers.\n   - Variations among prehistoric fish species were great, so Tiktaalik would not have stood out as unusual.\n   - Tiktaalik\'s fingers were an important development in animal evolution.\n   - It is likely that Tiktaalik is an ancestor to many land animals with fingers.\n\n2. **Option Analysis**:\n   - **Option A**: "Tiktaalik is not the ancestor of any currently surviving fish species."\n     - The context does not provide any information about the current survival status of Tiktaalik\'s descendants. It only mentions that Tiktaalik is an ancestor to many land animals with fingers, but it does not specify if these descendants are still alive.\n     - This option cannot be definitively supported by the given information.\n\n   - **Option B**: "Tiktaalik\'s fingers were its only feature to play a significant role in the development of modern land animals."\n     - The context states that Tiktaalik\'s fingers were an important development in animal evolution, but it does not specify that these were the only features. It only mentions that Tiktaalik is an ancestor to many land animals with fingers, implying that fingers were significant, but not necessarily the only feature.\n     - This option is not strongly supported by the given information.\n\n   - **Option C**: "The evolutionary significance of Tiktaalik could not be determined just through comparison to fish species of its time."\n     - The context mentions that variations among prehistoric fish species were great, so Tiktaalik would not have stood out as unusual. This implies that comparing Tiktaalik to other fish species of its time would not reveal its evolutionary significance.\n     - This option aligns with the context, as it suggests that Tiktaalik\'s importance could only be recognized by understanding its role in the broader evolutionary context, not just by comparing it to other fish species of its time.\n\n   - **Option D**: "No fish without fingers would ever be able to move on land."\n     - The context does not provide any information about the ability of fish without fingers to move on land. It only mentions that Tiktaalik\'s fingers were important in the development of land animals.\n     - This option cannot be definitively supported by the given information.\nThe correct option is:']
