n2. **Option B:**\n   - Trees: 150 trees \u00d7 $50/tree = $7500\n   - Benches: 75 benches \u00d7 $100/bench = $7500\n   - Walking paths: 30 walking paths \u00d7 $200/walking path = $6000\n   - Total cost for Option B: $7500 + $7500 + $6000 = $19000\n\nNow, we compare the total costs:\n- Total cost for Option A: $14000\n- Total cost for Option B: $19000\n\nSince $14000 is less than $19000, Option A is the more economical choice.\nThe council should choose Option A to minimize the total cost.\nThe correct option is: A\n</think>\n<answer>\nA\n</answer>",
