relate to the aging process of the cloned sheep in the study. It does not provide evidence that cloning affects the aging process. Thus, it does not weaken the conclusion.\n\nC) The current somatic cell cloning technology is far from perfect.\n- This option suggests that the cloning process itself might be flawed, but it does not provide evidence that the cloned sheep are aging abnormally. It does not directly address the conclusion about the aging process. Therefore, it does not weaken the conclusion.\n\nD) The researchers did not examine the major molecular markers associated with aging.\n- This option is crucial. If the researchers did not examine the major molecular markers associated with aging, it means that they might not have detected any significant differences in the aging process between the cloned sheep and the control group. This would cast doubt on the conclusion that the cloning process does not affect the aging process. If there are indeed molecular markers associated with aging that were not examined, it could mean that the cloned sheep are aging differently, even if the visible symptoms are mild.\nThe correct option is:"]
