messages:   32%|###1      | 190/600 [1:20:55<1:25:29, 12.51s/it]['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn the process of accompanying their children, many parents will encounter the problem of their children lying or concealing the truth. Lying is almost what many parents are most worried about. Their children\'s bad behavior is even more frightening and angry than their children\'s poor academic performance.If we say that many parents have not solved the problem of their children lying well, at least most of them should pay attention to it, while the problem of children concealing their own situation from their parents is not only worse solved, but also not given enough attention.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is true of the original text?\n# Options:\nA) Parents think that children\'s failure to report information is more worrying than lying\nB) Parents believe that lying is the most unforgivable moral problem\nC) Most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying\nD) Children\'s behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and question step by step:\n\n1. **Context Analysis**:\n   - The context discusses the concerns of parents regarding their children\'s behavior.\n   - It specifically mentions that lying is a significant concern for parents.\n   - The text states that parents are more worried about their children\'s bad behavior than their poor academic performance.\n   - It also mentions that the problem of children concealing their own situation from their parents is worse solved and not given enough attention.\n\n2. **Question Analysis**:\n   - The question asks which of the given options is true based on the information provided in the context.\n\n3. **Option Analysis**:\n   - **Option A**: "Parents think that children\'s failure to report information is more worrying than lying."\n     - The context does not explicitly state that parents think children concealing information is more worrying than lying. It only mentions that concealing information is worse solved and not given enough attention.\n   - **Option B**: "Parents believe that lying is the most unforgivable moral problem."\n     - The context does not provide information about parents\' beliefs regarding the severity of lying as a moral problem. It only mentions that lying is a significant concern.\n   - **Option C**: "Most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying."\n     - The context does not provide information about the willingness of parents to solve the problem of lying. It only mentions that many parents are worried about it.\n   - **Option D**: "Children\'s behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents."\n     - The context explicitly states that the problem of children concealing their own situation is worse solved and not given enough attention.\nThe correct option is:']
