result is one, it means that the event has occurred."\n     - This is incorrect because if the probability is one, the event is certain to occur, not necessarily that it has occurred.\n   - **Option C**: "When the probability of an event occurring as a result is zero, the event must occur."\n     - This is incorrect because if the probability is zero, the event is certain not to occur.\n   - **Option D**: "The probability of the risk must be zero or one."\n     - This is incorrect because the context states that uncertainty is between zero and one, not that the probability must be zero or one.\n\n3. **Conclusion**:\n   -\nThe correct option is:']
