messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnalogical argument is based on the sameness or similarity of two objects in some attributes, and infers that the two objects are also the same or similar in other attributes. Its logical form is that object A has the attributes of a, b, c and d. Object B has properties of a, b, c. So object B has the property of d.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the followings belongs to analogical argument?\n# Options:\nA) Tao yuanming does not bow for five buckets of rice, li bai does not destroy eyebrows and bend over power. this shows that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries\nB) Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation\nC) Compared with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work, comrade bethune is extremely responsible for his work and extremely enthusiastic towards his comrades and the people, which shows that comrade bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others\nD) Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the definition of an analogical argument and analyze each option to see which one fits the given definition. \n\n1. **Definition Recap**: An analogical argument is based on the sameness or similarity of two objects in some attributes, and infers that the two objects are also the same or similar in other attributes. It follows the logical form: Object A has attributes a, b, c, and d. Object B has attributes a, b, c. Therefore, Object B has attribute d.\n\n2. **Option Analysis**:\n   - **Option A**: "Tao Yuanming does not bow for five buckets of rice, Li Bai does not destroy eyebrows and bend over power. This shows that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries."\n     - This statement does not follow the form of an analogical argument. It does not compare two specific objects (A and B) with attributes and then infer a similarity in another attribute. Instead, it makes a generalization about ambitious people based on two historical figures.\n   - **Option B**: "Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction, and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation."\n     - This statement does not fit the form of an analogical argument either. It does not compare two specific objects with attributes and then infer a similarity in another attribute. Instead, it makes a generalization about the properties of light and sound.\n   - **Option C**: "Compared with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work, Comrade Bethune is extremely responsible for his work and extremely enthusiastic towards his comrades and the people, which shows that Comrade Bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others."\n     - This statement does not fit the form of an analogical argument. It does not compare two specific objects with attributes and then infer a similarity in another attribute. Instead, it makes a generalization about Comrade Bethune based on his behavior compared to others.\n   - **Option D**: "Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper."\n     - This statement fits the form of an analogical argument. It compares two specific objects (silver and copper) with attributes (electrical conductivity) and then infers a similarity in another attribute (suitability as a conductive material) based on a different attribute (resistivity).\nThe correct option is:']
