tly understood based on the passage.\n\n### Option Analysis:\n**A) The new material can greatly reduce the indoor temperature**\n- The context does not mention anything about indoor temperature reduction. It specifically talks about the reflectivity of urban roofs and road surfaces, which affect outdoor temperatures.\n- Therefore, this option is incorrect.\n\n**B) Urban road surface accounts for more than half of the total urban area**\n- The context explicitly states that roofs and roads account for more than 60% of the city's surface area.\n- This statement is correct according to the passage.\n\n**C) People are exploring new ways to alleviate global warming**\n- While the passage does suggest a method to reduce global warming (improving reflectivity), it does not explicitly state that people are exploring new ways to alleviate global warming.\n- This option is not directly supported by the given information.\n\n**D) The surface of dark materials has strong reflectivity**\n- The passage does not provide any information about the reflectivity of dark materials. It only mentions the reflectivity of light-colored materials.\n- Therefore, this option is incorrect.\nThe correct option is:"]
