messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nMost people who drink too much will have a headache. If Xiao Wang doesn\'t drink too much, he probably won\'t have a headache.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is similar to the above reasoning?\n# Options:\nA) Most greyhounds are easy to train, so xiao wang must have no problem training his new dog\nB) Most domestic cars are very poor, this car is well done, so it may not be domestic\nC) Most famous actors perform very well, because lao gao is not a famous actor, so he may not act well\nD) Most engineers have studied in school for many years, so lao liu may be an engineer because he has studied in school for many years\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step.\nFirst, let\'s analyze the given context:\n1. Most people who drink too much will have a headache.\n2. If Xiao Wang doesn\'t drink too much, he probably won\'t have a headache.\nFrom these statements, we can infer a conditional relationship:\n- If someone drinks too much, they will likely have a headache.\n- If someone doesn\'t drink too much, they probably won\'t have a headache.\nNow, let\'s look at the question: "Based on the above information, which of the following is similar to the above reasoning? "\nWe need to find an option that follows a similar conditional relationship.\nLet\'s examine each option:\nA) Most greyhounds are easy to train, so Xiao Wang must have no problem training his new dog.\n- This option introduces a new premise (greyhounds are easy to train) and a conclusion (Xiao Wang must have no problem training his dog). This does not follow the conditional relationship given in the context.\nB) Most domestic cars are very poor, this car is well done, so it may not be domestic.\n- This option introduces a new premise (domestic cars are very poor) and a conclusion (the car may not be domestic). This does not follow the conditional relationship given in the context.\nC) Most famous actors perform very well, because Lao Gao is not a famous actor, so he may not act well.\n- This option introduces a new premise (famous actors perform very well) and a conclusion (Lao Gao may not act well). This does not follow the conditional relationship given in the context.\nD) Most engineers have studied in school for many years, so Lao Liu may be an engineer because he has studied in school for many years.\n- This option introduces a new premise (most engineers have studied in school for many years) and a conclusion (Lao Liu may be an engineer). This follows a similar conditional relationship to the given context.\nThe correct option is:']
