messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nTo reduce the frequency of ground collisions, Innovair will begin giving its ground crews additional training, at an annual cost of $500, 000. Although this will cut the number of ground collisions by about half at best, the drop in repair costs can be expected to be much greater, since __ .\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following most logically completes the argument? In a typical year, Innovair\'s airplanes are involved in 35 collisions while parked or being towed in airports, with a resulting yearly cost of $1, 000, 000 for repairs.\n# Options:\nA) Most ground collisions have been caused by the least experienced ground-crew members\nB) A ground collision typically occurs when there are no passengers on the airplane\nC) The additional training will focus on helping ground crews avoid those kinds of ground collisions that cause the most costly damage\nD) The $500, 000 cost figure for the additional training of ground crews includes the wages that those crews will earn during the time spent in actual training\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step:\n\n1. **Context Analysis**:\n   - Innovair will start giving its ground crews additional training, which will cost $500, 000 annually.\n   - This training is expected to reduce the number of ground collisions by about half.\n   - The drop in repair costs is expected to be much greater than the cost of the training.\n\n2. **Question Analysis**:\n   - We need to complete the argument by providing a reason why the drop in repair costs will be much greater than the cost of the training.\n   - The context provides information about the current situation:\n     - 35 ground collisions occur annually.\n     - Each collision results in a repair cost of $1, 000, 000.\n     - Therefore, the total annual repair cost is $1, 000, 000.\n\n3. **Option Analysis**:\n   - **Option A**: "Most ground collisions have been caused by the least experienced ground-crew members."\n     - This option does not directly address the repair cost reduction. It only provides information about the cause of collisions.\n   - **Option B**: "A ground collision typically occurs when there are no passengers on the airplane."\n     - This option is irrelevant to the repair cost reduction and does not provide a logical reason for the greater cost savings.\n   - **Option C**: "The additional training will focus on helping ground crews avoid those kinds of ground collisions that cause the most costly damage."\n     - This option directly addresses the repair cost reduction. If the training focuses on avoiding the most costly collisions, it would logically result in a greater reduction in repair costs compared to the cost of the training.\n   - **Option D**: "The $500, 000 cost figure for the additional training of ground crews includes the wages that those crews will earn during the time spent in actual training."\n     - This option is about the cost structure of the training and does not provide a reason for the greater cost savings in repair costs.\nThe correct option is:']
