messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA Beijing newspaper, entitled 15% of fathers raise children for others, released statistics from a judicial material evidence appraisal center in Beijing: of the nearly 600 people who conducted paternity tests in Beijing within a year, 15% of the test results excluded paternity.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings does not question the reliability of statistical inference?\n# Options:\nA) The title of the article should be limited: 15% of the fathers who carry out paternity tests raise children for others.\nB) When the paternity test is conducted, there are already doubts about the paternity relationship.\nC) Can modern science and technology really accurately identify paternity?\nD) The cost of paternity testing is too high.\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step.\n\n1. **Context Analysis**:\n   - The context provides information about a Beijing newspaper article.\n   - The article states that out of nearly 600 paternity tests conducted in Beijing in a year, 15% of the test results excluded paternity.\n   - This implies that 15% of the fathers tested were found not to be the biological fathers of the children.\n\n2. **Question Analysis**:\n   - The question asks which option does not question the reliability of the statistical inference.\n   - Statistical inference involves drawing conclusions about a population based on a sample.\n   - The reliability of the inference depends on the sample being representative and the accuracy of the tests.\n\n3. **Option Analysis**:\n   - **Option A**: "The title of the article should be limited: 15% of the fathers who carry out paternity tests raise children for others."\n     - This option is not questioning the reliability of the statistical inference. It is merely suggesting a possible interpretation of the title.\n   - **Option B**: "When the paternity test is conducted, there are already doubts about the paternity relationship."\n     - This option questions the reliability of the statistical inference because it suggests that the tests themselves may not be accurate or reliable.\n   - **Option C**: "Can modern science and technology really accurately identify paternity?"\n     - This option questions the reliability of the statistical inference by questioning the accuracy of the testing methods.\n   - **Option D**: "The cost of paternity testing is too high."\n     - This option questions the reliability of the statistical inference by suggesting that the high cost might affect the sample size or the representativeness of the tests.\nThe correct option is:']
