messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn public speeches, some people talk long and talk endlessly; some people condense their meaning into one sentence, and this sentence is like a heavy stone, stirring up waves in the calm mind of the audience It is commendable and memorable. On October 19, 1936, at the meeting of people from all walks of life in Shanghai to sacrifice Lu Xun, my country\'s famous journalist, politician, and social activist Mr. Zou Taofen delivered a speech of only 33 words: Not too soon, I would like to commemorate Mr. with one sentence: Many people have fallen without a fight, and Mr. Lu Xun has fallen without a fight.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the main expression of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Short speeches, such as zou taofen\'s one-sentence speech, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects\nB) The phrase unyielding in battle accurately outlines mr. lu xun\'s fighting spirit\nC) The word war contains how much people admire and praise mr. lu xun\nD) Many shameless literati not only do not fight, but also slave their hands and knees; but the gentleman\'s eyebrows are cold and stubborn\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step:\n\n1. **Context Analysis**:\n   - The context discusses different types of speeches in public settings.\n   - It mentions that some speeches are long and drawn out, while others are concise and impactful.\n   - It specifically highlights Zou Taofen\'s speech on October 19, 1936, at a meeting in Shanghai.\n   - Zou Taofen\'s speech was only 33 words long and was delivered at a memorial for Lu Xun.\n   - The speech was described as a "heavy stone" that stirred up waves in the audience.\n\n2. **Question Analysis**:\n   - The question asks for the main expression of the text.\n   - We need to identify which option best captures the essence of the text.\n\n3. **Option Analysis**:\n   - **Option A**: "Short speeches, such as Zou Taofen\'s one-sentence speech, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects."\n     - This option aligns well with the context, which praises Zou Taofen\'s speech for its brevity and impact.\n   - **Option B**: "The phrase \'unyielding in battle\' accurately outlines Mr. Lu Xun\'s fighting spirit."\n     - While this option mentions Lu Xun\'s fighting spirit, it doesn\'t capture the main expression of the text about speeches.\n   - **Option C**: "The word \'war\' contains how much people admire and praise Mr. Lu Xun."\n     - This option focuses on the word "war" and its implications, but it doesn\'t encapsulate the main idea about speeches.\n   - **Option D**: "Many shameless literati not only do not fight, but also slave their hands and knees; but the gentleman\'s eyebrows are cold and stubborn."\n     - This option seems to be a separate statement about Lu Xun and other literati, which is not directly related to the main expression of the text about speeches.\nThe correct option is:']
