messages:   55%|#####5    | 330/600 [2:18:03<39:57,  8.88s/it]['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn most cases, writing poems and filling words is a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion. It is unpredictable for a beginner to have what kind of feelings and choose what kind of sentence pattern to start with. But once he has a preliminary idea, he can always get appropriate help in the book Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms. He will know which words are suitable to express what kind of feelings, what kind of rhyme he should choose, and how to make rational use of certain rhetorical devices so as not to be fooled in the face of special syntax. If you have read enough ancient poems and have a certain sense of language, you will indeed be able to complete your first creation with the help of this book. It can not teach people to write amazing masterpieces, but with the greatest sincerity to prevent you from making all kinds of jokes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings is the main content of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones\nB) Poetry creation is essentially a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion\nC) Tang and song poetry rhythms provides a very good help for beginners\nD) The creator of poetry must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishment\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and analyze each option step by step:\n\n1. **Context Analysis**:\n   - The passage discusses the process of writing poems and the role of Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms.\n   - It emphasizes that writing poems is a mutual accommodation between language and emotion.\n   - It mentions that beginners might struggle with choosing appropriate feelings and sentence patterns.\n   - The book Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms provides guidance on suitable words, rhyme, and rhetorical devices.\n   - It states that with enough reading and language sense, beginners can use the book to create their first poems.\n   - The book does not aim to teach amazing masterpieces but helps prevent beginners from making mistakes.\n\n2. **Option Analysis**:\n   - **Option A**: "Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones"\n     - While the passage mentions that the book provides guidance on suitable words and rhyme, it does not specifically highlight the "rich tones" as the main reason for its suitability.\n   - **Option B**: "Poetry creation is essentially a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion"\n     - This statement is true according to the passage, but it is not the main content. It is a supporting idea.\n   - **Option C**: "Tang and song poetry rhythms provides a very good help for beginners"\n     - This option aligns well with the passage\'s main message. It emphasizes the book\'s role in helping beginners navigate the process of writing poems.\n   - **Option D**: "The creator of poetry must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishment"\n     - This is not supported by the passage. The text does not claim that creators must have abundant emotion or high literary accomplishment to write poetry.\nThe correct option is:']
