messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn recent years, community banks in some big cities have been closed frequently. At the same time, a series of new banks, such as unmanned banks, 5G banks and smart banks, keep emerging. Bank branches are bidding farewell to cold glass counters and metal benches. The traditional transaction processing functions of bank branches are weakened, and customized services, product experience, social interaction and other functions are increasingly prominent. As a result, some experts predict that traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings, if true, best supports the expert's view?\n# Options:\nA) Customers need to enter the door to take the number, wait for the number, to deal with a simple business cost a long time\nB) The introduction of artificial intelligence and other technological means has changed people's impression of bank branches\nC) Complex business must be signed face to face at the bank branch, such as account opening, account cancellation, etc., must be handled by myself and manual audit\nD) Online banking, mobile banking and other emerging, bank outlets as the main channel of service is weakening\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option best supports the expert's view that traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years. Let's analyze each option step by step:\n\nA) Customers need to enter the door to take the number, wait for the number, to deal with a simple business cost a long time.\n- This option highlights a negative aspect of traditional bank branches, such as long wait times and the need to physically visit. While it may indicate inconvenience, it does not directly support the idea that branches will disappear.\n\nB) The introduction of artificial intelligence and other technological means has changed people's impression of bank branches.\n- This option suggests that technological advancements are altering how people perceive bank branches. This could imply that branches are becoming less relevant as customers prefer more convenient and efficient alternatives. This aligns well with the expert's view that traditional branches will disappear.\n\nC) Complex business must be signed face to face at the bank branch, such as account opening, account cancellation, etc., must be handled by myself and manual audit.\n- This option highlights specific tasks that require face-to-face interaction, which are still necessary in traditional branches. It does not support the idea that branches will disappear, as it suggests that certain functions are still important.\n\nD) Online banking, mobile banking and other emerging, bank outlets as the main channel of service is weakening.\n- This option indicates that online and mobile banking are becoming more prevalent and are reducing the importance of bank outlets. This supports the expert's view that traditional branches will disappear, as it suggests a shift away from physical branches.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, both B and D seem to support the expert's view. However, option B provides a broader context by mentioning the overall impact of technology on people's perception of bank branches, which is more comprehensive and aligns better with the expert's prediction of a significant shift.\nThe correct option is:"]
