      "text": " B) 15%<|User|>Here's another logical reasoning problem for you.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n# Context:\nA survey was conducted to assess the satisfaction levels of customers with a new product. The survey results are summarized in the following table:\n\n| Satisfaction Level | Number of Customers |\n|--------------------|---------------------|\n| Very Satisfied      | 120                 |\n| Satisfied           | 240                 |\n| Neutral             | 90                  |\n| Dissatisfied        | 30                  |\n| Very Dissatisfied   | 10                  |\n\n# Question:\nWhat percentage of the total customers surveyed were very satisfied with the new product?\n# Options:\nA) 25%\nB) 30%\nC) 33%\nD) 40%<|Assistant|<think>\nTo determine the percentage of the total customers who were very satisfied with the new product, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of customers surveyed:**\n   - Very Satisfied: 120 customers\n   - Satisfied: 240 customers\n   - Neutral: 90 customers\n   - Dissatisfied: 30 customers\n   - Very Dissatisfied: 10 customers\n\n   Adding these together:\n   \\[\n   120 + 240 + 90 + 30 + 10 = 490 \\text{ customers}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the number of very satisfied customers:**\n   - Very Satisfied: 120 customers\n\n3. **Calculate the percentage of very satisfied customers:**\n   - The formula to calculate the percentage is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Number of Very Satisfied Customers}}{\\text{Total Number of Customers}} \\right) \\times 100\n     \\]\n   - Plugging in the values:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{120}{490} \\right) \\times 100\n     \\]\n\n4. **Perform the division and multiplication:**\n   - First, divide 120 by 490:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{120}{490} \\approx 0.2449\n     \\]\n   - Then, multiply by 100 to convert to a percentage:\n     \\[\n     0.2449 \\times 100 \\approx 24.49\\%\n     \\]\n\n5. **Round to the nearest whole number:**\n   - 24.49% rounds to 25%.\n\nTherefore, the percentage of the total customers who were very satisfied with the new product is approximately 25%.\n\nThe correct answer is:\nA) 25%<|Assistant|>",
