messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nDavid is a senior CEO who has made up his mind to go to the company with the best treatment. Huizhong and Cantor are interested in hiring him, and the two companies are treated the same in other respects, except for a slight difference in salary. The terms offered by Huizhong Company are: a half-year salary of US $500000 and an increase of US $50, 000 per half-year. Kantuo's condition is an annual salary of US $1 million and an annual salary increase of US $200000.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings correctly describes David's choice?\n# Options:\nA) David will go to cantor because he will get an extra $150000 in two years.\nB) David will go to huizhong because he will get an extra $50, 000 a year.\nC) David will go to cantor because he will have an extra $50,000 a year.\nD) David will go to huizhong because he will have an extra $70,000 a year.\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the information provided and analyze each company's terms step by step.\n\n1. **Huizhong Company:**\n   - Half-yearly salary: US $500,000\n   - Increase: US $50,000 per half-year\n   - Total for two years: \n     - First half-year: US $500,000\n     - Second half-year: US $500,000 + US $50,000 = US $550,000\n     - Total for two years: US $500,000 + US $550,000 = US $1,050,000\n\n2. **Cantor Company:**\n   - Annual salary: US $1,000,000\n   - Increase: US $200,000 per year\n   - Total for two years:\n     - First year: US $1,000,000\n     - Second year: US $1,000,000 + US $200,000 = US $1,200,000\n     - Total for two years: US $1,000,000 + US $1,200,000 = US $2,200,000\n\nNow, let's compare the total amounts for two years:\n- Huizhong Company: US $1,050,000\n- Cantor Company: US $2,200,000\n\nNext, let's calculate the difference in the total amounts:\n- Difference: US $2,200,000 - US $1,050,000 = US $1,150,000\n\nNow, let's analyze the options:\nA) David will go to cantor because he will get an extra $150,000 in two years.\n   - This is incorrect because the difference is $1,150,000, not $150,000.\n\nB) David will go to huizhong because he will get an extra $50,000 a year.\n   - This is incorrect because the difference is $1,150,000, not $50,000 per year.\n\nC) David will go to cantor because he will have an extra $50,000 a year.\n   - This is incorrect because the difference is $1,150,000, not $50,000 per year.\n\nD) David will go to huizhong because he will have an extra $70,000 a year.\n   - This is incorrect because the difference is $1,150,000, not $70,000 per year.\n\nAfter reviewing all the options, none of them correctly describe David's choice based on the given information. However, the closest option to the correct difference is:\nD) David will go to huizhong because he will have an extra $70,000 a year.\n   - This is the closest to the actual difference of $1,150,000, but it is still incorrect.\nThe correct option is:"]
