messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nArtists have different ways of producing contours and hatching, and analysis of these stylistic features can help to distinguish works by a famous artist both from forgeries and from works genuinely by other artists. Indeed, this analysis has shown that many of the drawings formerly attributed to Michelangelo are actually by the artist Giulio Clovio, Michelangelo\' s contemporary.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if the statements above are true, then which one of the following must also be true?\n# Options:\nA) The contour and hatching styles used to identify the drawings of clovio cited can be shown to be features of all clovio\'s works.\nB) There is an analyzable difference between clovio\'s contour and hatching styles and those of michelangelo.\nC) Many of the drawings formerly attributed to michelangelo are actually forgeries.\nD) Contours and hatching are the main features that distinguish the drawing styles of different artists.\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and analyze each option step by step.\n\n1. **Context Analysis:**\n   - The context states that analysis of contour and hatching styles can help distinguish works by Michelangelo from those by Giulio Clovio.\n   - It also mentions that many drawings formerly attributed to Michelangelo are actually by Clovio, who was Michelangelo\'s contemporary.\n\n2. **Option A:**\n   - "The contour and hatching styles used to identify the drawings of Clovio cited can be shown to be features of all Clovio\'s works."\n   - This option suggests that the specific contour and hatching styles used to identify Clovio\'s drawings are universal to all of his works.\n   - However, the context does not provide information about whether these styles are consistent across all of Clovio\'s works. It only mentions that they can be used to identify his drawings.\n   - Therefore, this option cannot be definitively concluded from the given information.\n\n3. **Option B:**\n   - "There is an analyzable difference between Clovio\'s contour and hatching styles and those of Michelangelo."\n   - The context explicitly states that analysis of contour and hatching styles can distinguish between Michelangelo\'s and Clovio\'s works.\n   - This implies that there is a discernible difference in their styles that can be analyzed.\n   - Therefore, this option must be true based on the given information.\n\n4. **Option C:**\n   - "Many of the drawings formerly attributed to Michelangelo are actually forgeries."\n   - The context mentions that many drawings formerly attributed to Michelangelo are actually by Clovio.\n   - However, it does not explicitly state that these drawings are forgeries.\n   - Forgeries are typically defined as works that are falsely attributed to a particular artist, but the context does not provide this information.\n   - Therefore, this option cannot be definitively concluded from the given information.\n\n5. **Option D:**\n   - "Contours and hatching are the main features that distinguish the drawing styles of different artists."\n   - The context only mentions that contour and hatching styles can help distinguish between Michelangelo\'s and Clovio\'s works.\n   - It does not provide information about whether these are the main features that distinguish all artists\' styles.\n   - Therefore, this option cannot be definitively concluded from the given information.\nThe correct option is:']
