      "text": "B<\uff5cUser\uff5c>\n<think>\nAfter analyzing each option, we can conclude that the correct answer is B. The definition explicitly mentions that agricultural antibiotics are allowed in the context of pollution-free vegetables. This directly aligns with the given information and does not require additional assumptions or interpretations.\n\nOption A is incorrect because the definition does not mandate the use of microbial pesticides.\nOption C is incorrect because it omits the requirement of low residue, which is a key criterion for pollution-free vegetables.\nOption D is incorrect because the definition only guarantees that the pesticide residue is below the allowable standard, not that the vegetables will never harm the body.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB\n</answer>",
