messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn our solar system only one of the nine planets -- Earth -- qualifies as fit to sustain life. Nonetheless, using this ratio, and considering the astonishingly large number of planetary systems in the universe, we must conclude that the number of planets fit to sustain some form of life is extremely large.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, the argument is questionable because it presumes which one of the following without providing justification?\n# Options:\nA) Life similar to earth\'s could evolve under conditions very different from those on earth.\nB) If a planet is earthlike, then life will arise on it.\nC) Our solar system is similar to many other planetary systems in the universe.\nD) Most other planetary systems in the universe have nine planets.\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step.\n\n1. **Context Analysis**:\n   - The context states that Earth is the only planet in our solar system that can sustain life.\n   - It then uses this ratio to argue that given the vast number of planetary systems in the universe, the number of planets that can sustain life must be extremely large.\n\n2. **Question Analysis**:\n   - The question asks us to identify the assumption that the argument presumes without providing justification.\n\n3. **Option Analysis**:\n   - **Option A**: "Life similar to earth\'s could evolve under conditions very different from those on earth."\n     - This option suggests that life could arise in conditions different from Earth\'s. The context does not make this assumption; it only states that Earth is the only planet that can sustain life.\n   - **Option B**: "If a planet is earthlike, then life will arise on it."\n     - This option directly states that life will arise on planets that are similar to Earth. The context does not make this assumption; it only states that Earth is the only planet that can sustain life.\n   - **Option C**: "Our solar system is similar to many other planetary systems in the universe."\n     - This option suggests that our solar system is representative of other planetary systems. The context does not make this assumption; it only discusses the number of planetary systems in the universe.\n   - **Option D**: "Most other planetary systems in the universe have nine planets."\n     - This option makes a specific claim about the number of planets in other planetary systems. The context does not make this assumption; it only discusses the number of planetary systems in the universe.\nThe correct option is:']
