ake it easier to plan events several years in advance, as the day of the week would be predictable. The other groups (religious observances and work schedules) are not directly impacted by the change in the calendar structure.\n\nTo summarize, the proposed change would make it easier for people who have to plan events several years in advance to predict the day of the week for specific dates, making their planning more consistent and predictable. The other groups are already affected by the current system and would not be directly impacted by the proposed change. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>I hope this clarifies why the other options are not directly affected by the proposed change. If you have any more questions, feel free to ask! <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for the detailed explanation. It really helps to understand why the other options are not affected by the proposed change. Could you also provide an example to illustrate how the proposed change would make planning events easier for people who have to plan several years in advance?\n<think>\nCertainly! Let's provide an example to illustrate how the proposed change would make planning events easier for people who have to plan several years in advance.\n\n### Example:\nSuppose you are planning a large event that requires a specific day of the week to occur. For instance, you need the event to fall on a Sunday to ensure it aligns with a specific religious observance or to maximize attendance.\n\n",
