should be lifelike"\n     - The passage explicitly mentions that history education should be integrated into life and should be "infiltrate into the neighborhoods and scenes of our lives in a rich and appropriate form."\n   - **Option C**: "History education is available anytime, anywhere"\n     - The passage does not specifically state that history education is available anytime, anywhere. It emphasizes integration into life but does not cover the availability aspect.\n   - **Option D**: "History exists in the collective memory of the nation"\n     - While the passage mentions that history education should be transformed into the collective memory of the nation, it does not directly summarize this point.\nThe correct option is:']
