messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nZhao Ming, Qian Hong and Sun Jie were admitted to Peking University, Tsinghua University and Beijing normal University. About which school they were admitted to, the students made the following guesses: classmate A guessed: Zhao Ming was admitted by Tsinghua University and Sun Jie was admitted by Beijing normal University. Classmate B guess: Zhao Ming was admitted by Beijing normal University and Qian Hong was admitted by Tsinghua University. Classmate C guess: Zhao Ming was admitted to Peking University and Sun Jie was admitted to Tsinghua University. As a result, the students' guesses were half right.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is their correct admission?\n# Options:\nA) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to peking university, tsinghua university and beijing normal university respectively.\nB) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to tsinghua university, beijing normal university and peking university respectively.\nC) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to beijing normal university, tsinghua university and peking university respectively.\nD) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to peking university, beijing normal university and tsinghua university respectively.\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the information and analyze the guesses step by step:\n\n1. **Identify the guesses:**\n   - Classmate A: Zhao Ming (Peking University), Sun Jie (Beijing Normal University)\n   - Classmate B: Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal University), Qian Hong (Tsinghua University)\n   - Classmate C: Zhao Ming (Peking University), Sun Jie (Tsinghua University)\n\n2. **Understand the condition:**\n   - The students' guesses are half right. This means that for each guess, exactly one part is correct and the other part is incorrect.\n\n3. **Analyze each guess:**\n   - **Guess A (Classmate A):**\n     - Zhao Ming (Peking University) is correct.\n     - Sun Jie (Beijing Normal University) is incorrect.\n     - This means Zhao Ming is admitted to Peking University and Sun Jie is not admitted to Beijing Normal University.\n   \n   - **Guess B (Classmate B):**\n     - Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal University) is incorrect.\n     - Qian Hong (Tsinghua University) is correct.\n     - This means Zhao Ming is not admitted to Beijing Normal University and Qian Hong is admitted to Tsinghua University.\n   \n   - **Guess C (Classmate C):**\n     - Zhao Ming (Peking University) is correct.\n     - Sun Jie (Tsinghua University) is incorrect.\n     - This means Zhao Ming is admitted to Peking University and Sun Jie is not admitted to Tsinghua University.\n\n4. **Combine the information:**\n   - From Guess A, Zhao Ming is admitted to Peking University.\n   - From Guess B, Qian Hong is admitted to Tsinghua University.\n   - From Guess C, Sun Jie is not admitted to Tsinghua University.\n\n5. **Determine Sun Jie's admission:**\n   - Since Sun Jie is not admitted to Tsinghua University (from Guess C), and Zhao Ming is admitted to Peking University (from Guess A), Sun Jie must be admitted to Beijing Normal University (since the only remaining university is Beijing Normal University).\n\n6. **Verify the solution:**\n   - Zhao Ming (Peking University)\n   - Qian Hong (Tsinghua University)\n   - Sun Jie (Beijing Normal University)\n\nThis solution satisfies the condition that each guess is half right:\n- Guess A: Zhao Ming (Peking University) is correct, Sun Jie (Beijing Normal University) is incorrect.\n- Guess B: Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal University) is incorrect, Qian Hong (Tsinghua University) is correct.\n- Guess C: Zhao Ming (Peking University) is correct, Sun Jie (Tsinghua University) is incorrect.\nThe correct option is:"]
