messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThere are five teams taking part in the game. As for the result of the game, the spectators have the following comments: (1) the champion is either Shannan team or Jiangbei team. (2) the champion is neither Shanbei nor Jiangnan. (3) the champion is Jiangnan team. (4) the champion is not Shannan team.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, the result of the competition showed that only one argument was correct. Which of the following options is the champion?\n# Options:\nA) Shannan.\nB) Jiangnan.\nC) Shanbei.\nD) Jiangbei.\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s analyze the given statements and determine which one is correct based on the condition that only one of the statements is true. We will then use this information to deduce the champion team.\n\n1. **Statement 1:** The champion is either Shannan team or Jiangbei team.\n2. **Statement 2:** The champion is neither Shanbei nor Jiangnan team.\n3. **Statement 3:** The champion is Jiangnan team.\n4. **Statement 4:** The champion is not Shannan team.\n\nLet\'s evaluate each statement one by one:\n\n- **Statement 1:** "The champion is either Shannan team or Jiangbei team."\n  - If this statement is true, then the champion must be either Shannan or Jiangbei.\n  - If this statement is false, then the champion cannot be Shannan or Jiangbei.\n\n- **Statement 2:** "The champion is neither Shanbei nor Jiangnan team."\n  - If this statement is true, then the champion cannot be Shanbei or Jiangnan.\n  - If this statement is false, then the champion can be Shanbei or Jiangnan.\n\n- **Statement 3:** "The champion is Jiangnan team."\n  - If this statement is true, then the champion is Jiangnan.\n  - If this statement is false, then the champion is not Jiangnan.\n\n- **Statement 4:** "The champion is not Shannan team."\n  - If this statement is true, then the champion cannot be Shannan.\n  - If this statement is false, then the champion is Shannan.\n\nGiven that only one of these statements is true, we need to find a consistent scenario where exactly one statement is true and the others are false.\n\nLet\'s test each statement one by one:\n\n### Testing Statement 1:\n- If Statement 1 is true, then the champion is either Shannan or Jiangbei.\n- If Statement 1 is false, then the champion cannot be Shannan or Jiangbei.\n\n### Testing Statement 2:\n- If Statement 2 is true, then the champion cannot be Shanbei or Jiangnan.\n- If Statement 2 is false, then the champion can be Shanbei or Jiangnan.\n\n### Testing Statement 3:\n- If Statement 3 is true, then the champion is Jiangnan.\n- If Statement 3 is false, then the champion is not Jiangnan.\n\n### Testing Statement 4:\n- If Statement 4 is true, then the champion is not Shannan.\n- If Statement 4 is false, then the champion is Shannan.\nThe correct option is:']
