is option directly supports the context\'s claim that deep tillage is more deleterious to topsoil erosion. It aligns with the argument\'s premise that deep tillage is worse than no-till methods.\n   - **Option B**: "Topsoil erosion does not make farmers want to till more deeply."\n     - This option is irrelevant to the argument. The context does not discuss farmers\' motivations for tilling more deeply; it only mentions the consequences of deep tillage.\n   - **Option C**: "The most expensive farming methods employ topsoil aeration techniques other than deep tillage."\n     - This option introduces a new piece of information about the cost of farming methods, which is not relevant to the argument\'s core claim about the relative effects of different tillage methods on topsoil erosion.\n   - **Option D**: "Tilling by any method other than deep tillage is not a viable option."\n     - This option is too strong and not supported by the context. The context only states that deep tillage is deleterious and suggests no-till methods as a viable alternative, but it does not claim that no-till is the only viable option.\nThe correct option is:']
