l number of students surveyed: 200\n   - Number of students who preferred Mint = \\( 15\\% \\times 200 \\)\n   - \\( 15\\% = \\frac{15}{100} = 0.15 \\)\n   - Number of students who preferred Mint = \\( 0.15 \\times 200 = 30 \\)\n\n2. **Calculate the number of students who preferred Vanilla:**\n   - Percentage of students who preferred Vanilla: 25%\n   - Number of students who preferred Vanilla = \\( 25\\% \\times 200 \\)\n   - \\( 25\\% = \\frac{25}{100} = 0.25 \\)\n   - Number of students who preferred Vanilla = \\( 0.25 \\times 200 = 50 \\)\n\n3. **Add the number of students who preferred Mint and Vanilla:**\n   - Number of students who preferred Mint = 30\n   - Number of students who preferred Vanilla = 50\n   - Total number of students who preferred Mint or Vanilla = \\( 30 + 50 = 80 \\)\n\nTherefore, the number of students who preferred Mint or Vanilla is 80.\n\nThe correct option is:\n</think>\n<answer>\nC\n</answer>",
