messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nUniversity administrator: Any proposal for a new department will not be funded if there are fewer than 50 people per year available for hire in that field and the proposed department would duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in one of our existing departments. The proposed Area Studies Department will duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in our existing Anthropology Department. However, we will fund the new department.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the following statements follows logically from the university administrator\'s statements?\n# Options:\nA) If the proposed area studies department did not duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in anthropology, then the new department would not be funded.\nB) The proposed area studies department would not duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in any existing department other than anthropology.\nC) The field of area studies has fewer than 50 people per year available for hire.\nD) The field of area studies has at least 50 people per year available for hire.\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given context and analyze each statement step by step.\n\n1. **Context Analysis:**\n   - The university administrator has set two conditions for funding a new department:\n     a. There must be at least 50 people per year available for hire in the field.\n     b. The proposed department should not duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in any existing department.\n   - The proposed Area Studies Department will be funded despite duplicating more than 25 percent of the material covered in the Anthropology Department.\n\n2. **Question:**\n   - We need to determine which statement logically follows from the given information.\n\n3. **Option Analysis:**\n   - **Option A:** "If the proposed area studies department did not duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in anthropology, then the new department would not be funded."\n     - This statement is not necessarily true. The administrator states that the new department will be funded even though it duplicates more than 25 percent of the material in Anthropology. Therefore, this condition does not apply to the funding decision.\n   - **Option B:** "The proposed area studies department would not duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in any existing department other than anthropology."\n     - This statement is not mentioned or implied in the context. The administrator only specifies that the Area Studies Department duplicates more than 25 percent of the material in the Anthropology Department.\n   - **Option C:** "The field of area studies has fewer than 50 people per year available for hire."\n     - This statement contradicts the context. The administrator explicitly states that there must be at least 50 people per year available for hire in the field of Area Studies.\n   - **Option D:** "The field of area studies has at least 50 people per year available for hire."\n     - This statement aligns with the context. The administrator requires at least 50 people per year available for hire in the field of Area Studies, and the funding decision is made despite the duplication issue.\nThe correct option is:']
