messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn recent years, the postgraduate entrance examination continues to heat up. Correspondingly, all kinds of tutoring classes for postgraduate entrance examination emerge as the times require, especially English and political tutoring classes are almost a necessary choice for those who take the postgraduate entrance examination. Xiaozhuang, who has just started the job, is also going to take the postgraduate entrance examination, so Xiaozhuang must attend an English tutoring class.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options can best strengthen the above argument?\n# Options:\nA) If you attend an english tutoring class, you can pass the postgraduate entrance examination.\nB) Only those who intend to take the postgraduate entrance examination will attend the english tutoring class.\nC) Even if you attend an english tutoring class, you may not be able to pass the postgraduate entrance examination.\nD) If you do not attend the english tutoring class, you will not be able to pass the postgraduate entrance examination.\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step.\n\n1. **Context Analysis:**\n   - The postgraduate entrance examination is becoming more competitive.\n   - Tutoring classes, especially for English and political subjects, are becoming more prevalent.\n   - Xiaozhuang, who has just started a job, is planning to take the postgraduate entrance examination.\n   - The argument states that Xiaozhuang must attend an English tutoring class.\n\n2. **Question Analysis:**\n   - We need to find an option that best strengthens the argument that Xiaozhuang must attend an English tutoring class.\n\n3. **Option Analysis:**\n   - **Option A:** "If you attend an English tutoring class, you can pass the postgraduate entrance examination."\n     - This option suggests a direct correlation between attending an English tutoring class and passing the examination. However, it does not necessarily imply that Xiaozhuang must attend an English tutoring class to pass. It only indicates a possibility.\n   - **Option B:** "Only those who intend to take the postgraduate entrance examination will attend the English tutoring class."\n     - This option implies that attending an English tutoring class is a necessary condition for those who intend to take the examination. Since Xiaozhuang is planning to take the examination, this option supports the argument that he must attend an English tutoring class.\n   - **Option C:** "Even if you attend an English tutoring class, you may not be able to pass the postgraduate entrance examination."\n     - This option weakens the argument by suggesting that attending a tutoring class does not guarantee success. It does not strengthen the argument.\n   - **Option D:** "If you do not attend the English tutoring class, you will not be able to pass the postgraduate entrance examination."\n     - This option is a strong conditional statement that implies a necessity. If not attending the class means not passing, then attending the class is necessary. This directly supports the argument that Xiaozhuang must attend an English tutoring class.\nThe correct option is:']
