sea floor. While it mentions the accuracy of images, it does not directly address the knowledge scientists have about the sea floor compared to other environments.\n   - **Option B**: This option discusses the complexity of understanding ocean currents compared to air currents on land. It supports the idea that the sea floor is more complex and less understood, which aligns with the context.\n   - **Option C**: This option mentions the stability of sea-level temperature conditions and how sunlight cannot penetrate deep below sea level. This does not directly support the idea that scientists know less about the sea floor compared to other environments.\n   - **Option D**: This option states that very few people have seen detailed maps of the sea floor, even though such maps are available in libraries. This supports the idea that the sea floor is less studied and less understood, which aligns with the context.\n\n4. **Conclusion**:\n   - Both options B and D support the idea that scientists know less about the undersea environment than other environments. However, option B provides a more direct comparison between the sea floor and land environments, which is more relevant to the context.\n   - Option D, while it supports the idea, does not provide a direct comparison to other environments.\nThe correct option is:"]
