uels can lead to higher temperatures due to the greenhouse effect, which is a direct result of human activities impacting the environment.\n\nD) A coastal city reclaimed the sea to build an island, and a small town with a capacity of 70,000 people was built on the island.\n- This does not describe an environmental effect. This scenario describes a human-made change to the environment, specifically the creation of an artificial island and the establishment of a town. While it involves environmental changes, it is not an environmental effect in the context of the given definition, which refers to changes caused by natural processes or human activities.\nThe correct option is:"]
