messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nFrench President Nicolas Sarkozy officially announced his re-election campaign, launched the campaign slogan of strong France and promised to lead France out of the economic crisis.Sarkozy\'s campaign advertisement on the streets of Paris reads: only a strong France can protect your family.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the reasoning of this campaign slogan,  whicn of the following options is true:\n# Options:\nA) A weak france can\'t protect your family\nB) A strong france can protect your family\nC) France is weak because it does not protect the family\nD) If the family is protected, france will be strong\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the campaign slogan step by step.\n\n1. **Context Analysis**:\n   - Nicolas Sarkozy announced his re-election campaign.\n   - He launched the slogan "strong France" and promised to lead France out of the economic crisis.\n   - His campaign advertisement in Paris states: "only a strong France can protect your family."\n\n2. **Campaign Slogan Analysis**:\n   - The slogan "only a strong France can protect your family" implies that the strength of France is directly linked to the protection of families.\n   - This suggests that the slogan is making a conditional statement: if France is strong, then families are protected.\n\n3. **Logical Reasoning**:\n   - The slogan can be interpreted as a conditional statement: "If France is strong, then families are protected."\n   - This can be written in logical form as: \\( \\text{If } \\text{France is strong} \\rightarrow \\text{Families are protected} \\).\n\n4. **Evaluating the Options**:\n   - **Option A**: "A weak France can\'t protect your family."\n     - This option is not directly supported by the slogan. The slogan only states that a strong France can protect families, not that a weak France cannot protect families.\n   - **Option B**: "A strong France can protect your family."\n     - This option aligns with the slogan. The slogan explicitly states that a strong France can protect families.\n   - **Option C**: "France is weak because it does not protect the family."\n     - This option is a causal statement that is not supported by the slogan. The slogan does not imply causality; it only states a conditional relationship.\n   - **Option D**: "If the family is protected, France will be strong."\n     - This option is the converse of the conditional statement. The slogan states "if France is strong, then families are protected," but the converse "if families are protected, then France is strong" is not necessarily true based on the given information.\nThe correct option is:']
