messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nSelf depletion phenomenon is a phenomenon in which individuals' ability or willingness to conduct voluntary activities decline in the process of long-term work, including the decline in ability or willingness to control the environment, control themselves, make choices and initiate behaviors, and at the same time, job burnout, self depletion but no progress.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is self depletion phenomenon?\n# Options:\nA) Lee did not finish his doctoral thesis and continued to postpone it. as a result, he did not graduate from school for eight years\nB) Chen has worked as a deputy director of the magazine for 20 years, and although he has published some personal works, he has not been promoted\nC) Song mou do sales work for nearly ten years, although he changed four or five companies, but because the performance is average, the income has not changed\nD) Wang has been working as an archive administrator for 15 years. he feels numb to his work and has no desire to change the status quo and get promoted\n<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the definition of self-depletion and analyze each option to see which one aligns with the given definition. The definition states that self-depletion involves:\n1. A decline in ability or willingness to conduct voluntary activities.\n2. A decline in ability or willingness to control the environment, control oneself, make choices, and initiate behaviors.\n3. Job burnout.\n4. No progress.\n\nNow, let's examine each option:\n\nA) Lee did not finish his doctoral thesis and continued to postpone it. as a result, he did not graduate from school for eight years.\n- This option describes Lee's procrastination and lack of progress in his doctoral thesis. However, it does not mention any decline in his ability to control his environment, make choices, or initiate behaviors. It also does not indicate job burnout. Therefore, this does not fit the definition of self-depletion.\n\nB) Chen has worked as a deputy director of the magazine for 20 years, and although he has published some personal works, he has not been promoted.\n- This option describes Chen's lack of promotion despite his work and publications. However, it does not mention any decline in his ability to control his environment, make choices, or initiate behaviors. It also does not indicate job burnout. Therefore, this does not fit the definition of self-depletion.\n\nC) Song mou do sales work for nearly ten years, although he changed four or five companies, but because the performance is average, the income has not changed.\n- This option describes Song's average performance and lack of promotion despite changing companies. However, it does not mention any decline in his ability to control his environment, make choices, or initiate behaviors. It also does not indicate job burnout. Therefore, this does not fit the definition of self-depletion.\n\nD) Wang has been working as an archive administrator for 15 years. he feels numb to his work and has no desire to change the status quo and get promoted.\n- This option describes Wang's feelings of numbness and lack of desire to change his status quo in his work. This aligns with the definition of self-depletion as it mentions:\n  - A decline in ability or willingness to control the environment (feeling numb to his work).\n  - A decline in ability or willingness to make choices (no desire to change the status quo).\n  - No progress (lack of promotion despite long-term work).\nThe correct option is:"]
