and private donations. It does not explicitly state that the government should provide more funding. While the context supports the idea of zoos, it does not provide any information about government funding.\n   \n   - **Option C: All wild animals should be held in captivity.**\n     - The context does not support this extreme view. It mentions that zoos provide a space for viewing wild animals and save endangered species, but it does not advocate for the captivity of all wild animals.\n   \n   - **Option D: Wild animals should sometimes be held in captivity.**\n     - This option aligns with the context. The context mentions that zoos provide a space for viewing wild animals and save endangered species through breeding programs. This implies that there are situations where wild animals are held in captivity for conservation purposes.\nThe correct option is:"]
